---
title: Creamy Salmon Pasta Bake
description: A quick and healthy creamy salmon pasta bake with leeks, pasta, and a light crispy panko breadcrumb topping.
image: https://www.everydayhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Creamy-Salmon-Pasta-.jpg
source: https://www.everydayhealthyrecipes.com/salmon-leek-pasta-bake-asparagus/#recipe
servings: 5
---

= Pasta & Topping =
Cook @fusilli pasta{3%cups}(250g) al dente in salted water for about ~{4%minutes} after it reaches a boil. Drain and set aside.

In a non-stick pan, melt @unsalted butter{1%tbsp}(14g) (from total amount), add @panko breadcrumbs{10%tbsp}(60g), and toast over medium heat for a few minutes until golden, stirring continuously. Remove from heat and set aside.

Preheat the oven to 220°C.

= Sauce =
In a large non-stick pan, melt 1 tbsp unsalted butter, add @leeks{1%medium}(finely chopped), and cook gently until softened, about ~{5%minutes}. Do not let the leeks brown.

Add remaining @unsalted butter{1/2%tbsp}(7g) and @all-purpose flour{2 1/2%tbsp}(20g). Stir until the flour is thoroughly combined.

Gradually pour in @milk{2 3/4%cups}(660ml), stirring until smooth. Add @vegetable stock cube{1 1/2} and @Dijon mustard{1 1/2%tsp}(7.5ml). Cook, stirring continuously, until the mixture starts bubbling.

Remove from heat and stir in @fromage frais{4%tbsp}(60g) and @white pepper{} to taste.

= Assembly & Baking =
Spread the cooked pasta over the bottom of a medium casserole dish and place chunks of @salmon{350%g}(skinless, boneless, cooked) on top.

Pour the sauce over the pasta and salmon, stirring gently to distribute evenly.

Scatter the toasted panko breadcrumbs over the top.

Bake in the upper part of the preheated oven for ~{15%minutes} until golden and bubbling. Serve immediately.